@startuml practice-session
!theme plain
title One practice session, end to end (see docs/pyq/user-flows.md)

actor Student
participant "Practice screen\n/practice/[sessionId]" as Screen
participant "hooks/pyq\n(react-query)" as Hooks
participant "PyqDataSource\napi-adapter" as Source
participant "PyqController\n/api/pyq/*" as API
participant "PracticeService" as Practice
participant "PyqAccessService" as Access
database "Postgres\nschema pyq" as DB

== Start ==

Student -> Screen : choose a filter set / mode
Screen -> Hooks : useStartSession(params)
Hooks -> Source : createSession(input)
Source -> API : POST pyq/sessions
API -> Practice : start(userId, dto)
Practice -> DB : resolve question ids\n(explicit list, or matchingIds + shuffle)
Practice -> Access : assertCanAnswer(userId)
note right of Access
  Checked before the session row is written:
  starting a session the student cannot answer
  anything in is a dead end.
end note
Access -> DB : count attempts since start of India day
alt free allowance spent
  Access --> API : 403 PYQ_DAILY_LIMIT_REACHED
  API --> Source : error body { code, message, dailyLimit }
  Source --> Hooks : throw DailyLimitError
  Hooks -> Screen : toast with "See plans" -> /subscription
else allowed
  Practice -> DB : INSERT practice_sessions\n+ session_questions (position 0..n)
  Practice -> DB : re-read via get()
  Practice --> Source : session + questions (no answers)
  Source --> Hooks : SessionDetail
  Hooks -> Screen : router.push(/practice/{id}?i=0)
end

== Answering ==

Student -> Screen : select an option
Screen -> Hooks : useAnswer(sessionId).mutate
Hooks -> Source : answer(sessionId, questionId, optionId, timeSpentMs)
Source -> API : POST pyq/sessions/:id/answers
API -> Practice : answer(...)
Practice -> DB : load session (owner-scoped; another user's id is a 404)
Practice -> Practice : assertOpen — SUBMITTED, or past\ntimeLimitSec + 30s grace, is a 409
Practice -> DB : option belongs to the question?
Practice -> DB : existing attempt?

alt PRACTICE / CUSTOM, already answered
  Practice --> API : the stored attempt, unchanged
  note right of Practice
    Practice answers are final once the
    explanation has been shown — otherwise
    "change it to the right one" would
    inflate every score.
  end note
else first answer (any mode), or a changed TEST answer
  Practice -> Access : assertCanAnswer — only on a FIRST answer
  Practice -> DB : UPSERT attempts\n(selected_option_id, is_correct, time_spent_ms, answered_at)
end

alt mode == TEST and not yet submitted
  Practice --> Source : { questionId, selectedOptionId, recorded: true }
  Source --> Screen : palette marks it "answered"; no correctness
else PRACTICE / CUSTOM
  Practice -> DB : load question + options
  Practice --> Source : + isCorrect, correctOptionId,\nexplanation, explanationFigure
  Source --> Screen : reveal the answer inline
end
Hooks -> Hooks : invalidate ["pyq","user"]\n(access, stats, streak, lists)

== Flagging ==

Student -> Screen : flag for review
Screen -> Hooks : useSetFlag(sessionId)
Hooks -> Source : setFlag(...)
Source -> API : PATCH pyq/sessions/:id/questions/:qid/flag
API -> Practice : flag(...)
Practice -> DB : UPSERT attempts SET flagged\n(a row may exist with no selected option)
Practice --> Screen : { questionId, flagged }

== Submit and review ==

Student -> Screen : Submit
Screen -> Hooks : useSubmitSession()
Hooks -> Source : submitSession(sessionId)
Source -> API : POST pyq/sessions/:id/submit
API -> Practice : submit(...)
Practice -> DB : read attempts, score them
Practice -> DB : UPDATE practice_sessions\nWHERE status = IN_PROGRESS\nSET SUBMITTED, counts, accuracy
note right of Practice
  Conditional update, so submitting twice
  scores once and returns the same review.
end note
Practice -> Practice : review() — 409 unless SUBMITTED
Practice --> Source : full detail, answers and explanations revealed
Hooks -> Hooks : setQueryData for session + review,\nthen invalidate ["pyq","user"]
Screen -> Student : /results, then /review

Student -> Screen : open /review later
Screen -> Hooks : useSessionReview(sessionId)
Hooks -> Source : getReview(sessionId)
Source -> API : GET pyq/sessions/:id/review
API -> Practice : review(...)
Practice -> DB : session + session_questions + attempts
Practice --> Screen : same payload as submit

@enduml
